{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And the sense of <b>Bless, O YHWH, his army</b> is that they shall be a great host, and the meaning is that they shall multiply and not diminish when they come to the Sanctuary, in the same sense as <i>Do not cut off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites</i> (Numbers 4:18), and likewise it is stated in their warnings (ibid. verse 19), <i>that they not die</i>. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Deuteronomy 33:11) rendered <i>nisveih</i>, from the language of <i>all their livestock and all their wealth</i> (Numbers 31:9). He intends what our Rabbis said (Yoma 26a) concerning the incense offering, that it brings blessing, and it is attached to <i>they shall offer incense in Your nostrils</i>, for from it his wealth shall be blessed, as we learned (ibid.): fresh each day for the incense. And in the Sifre (Bereishit Rabbah? — no, Sifre on this verse): <b>Bless, O YHWH, his army</b> — in possessions; from here they said: most priests are wealthy. In the name of Abba derosh they said: <i>I have been young and now I am old, yet I have not seen a righteous man forsaken</i> (Psalms 37:25) — this refers to the seed of Aaron."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The citation 'בספרי (ברכה שנב)' refers to the Sifre on Deuteronomy, section 352. The phrase 'משום אבא דורש' is rendered 'in the name of Abba derosh' as a proper name/epithet."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:59:27.755090889Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}